<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Concepción del Uruguay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Concepción del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> is a city in Entre Ríos province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, on the Uruguay River, founded in 1783. In 1815 it hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-oriente">Congress of Oriente</a>, called by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Artigas</a> for the provinces of his Federal League. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Francisco Ramírez</a> made it the seat of his Republic of Entre Ríos in 1820, and it served as the provincial capital for much of the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/concepcion-del-uruguay.jpg" alt="Concepción del Uruguay" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Zarce~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Concepcion_del_Uruguay_plaza_Ramirez.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
